 "result_text": "The `defaults` parameter is now used instead of ignored. I haven't run it or any tests, so the change is untested.\n\nWhen a field named in the format string is missing from the log record, the formatter now uses the value from `defaults`. If the field isn't in `defaults` either, it still comes out as `None`, as before. The `defaults` values also go through `rename_fields`, because they are looked up in the same step as the other format fields.\n\nThe change is in `src/pythonjsonlogger/core.py`: the constructor stores `defaults`, and `add_fields` looks it up. I also updated the docstring, which used to say the parameter was ignored.\n\nI read the issue as \"make it behave like `logging.Formatter`'s `defaults`\". That covers fields named in the format string, so a default for a field that isn't in `fmt` is never added to the output. Say so if you want those added too.",
